look at the plan below and create the appropriate file structure basline. language is python, and were using streamlit for front end. fallow/
├── README.md
├── pyproject.toml
├── .env.example                 # LLM_API_KEY, SENSOR_MODE=mock|live
├── app.py                       # Streamlit entry (dashboard)
├── pages/
│   ├── 1_Inventory.py
│   └── 2_Grow.py
├── larder/
│   ├── models.py                # Pydantic: InventoryItem, SpoilageRisk, MealPlan, GrowPlan
│   ├── spoilage/
│   │   ├── predictor.py         # LLM call + heuristic fallback
│   │   └── shelf_life.py        # Static baseline table
│   ├── meals/planner.py
│   ├── grow/
│   │   ├── advisor.py
│   │   └── balance.py
│   ├── sensors/
│   │   ├── base.py              # SensorSnapshot model + Sensor protocol (the contract)
│   │   ├── mock.py
│   │   └── live.py              # Built last
│   ├── llm/
│   │   ├── client.py            # Retries, timeout, JSON validation
│   │   └── prompts.py
│   └── store.py                 # SQLite or JSON file
├── fixtures/
│   ├── inventory.sample.json
│   └── sensor.sample.json
├── tests/
│   ├── test_spoilage_fallback.py
│   └── test_planner_inventory_only.py
└── docs/
    ├── architecture.md
    └── demo-script.md . Description

Fallow is a survival-grade kitchen and garden planner. It tracks what’s in your pantry, uses an LLM to predict what will spoil first, and builds a cooking plan so nothing goes to waste. A pluggable sensor feed (location, weather, soil condition) then drives a grow plan that tells you what you can plant and how to balance your food supply for resilience. Nothing rots, nothing is wasted, everything is planned.
